 given for $kA$ in the problem statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 k & - 9 k & 10 k\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-12 & -54 & 60\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can solve for $k$ by equating any two corresponding (nonzero) elements. Let's choose the elements in row $1$ and column $2$, $- 9 k$ and $-54.$ Equating these elements, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}- 9 k & =-54 \\\\ k & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We would still get the same result if we chose any other two corresponding (nonzero) elements." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["71c0ea85-8283-576a-8299-6ae94d64a63b"] :db/ensure :question/validate} {:db/id "generator" :question-generator/id #uuid "b3722823-efb6-5ebe-bf0d-534c30b694f8" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186059741.py"} [:db/add 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/question-generator "generator"] {:db/id 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/questions ["f16bbe6e-f1a6-54a1-bc2e-dc02da0cf210"]} [:db/ensure 17592186059741 :knowledge-point/validate]]
